// Title: DriverQuery.EXE Execution
// ID: a20def93-0709-4eae-9bd2-31206e21e6b2
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-01-19
// Tags: attack.discovery
// Description: Detect usage of the "driverquery" utility. Which can be used to perform reconnaissance on installed drivers
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((process.executable endswith "driverquery.exe") or (process.pe.original_file_name == "drvqry.exe")) and not ((((process.parent.executable endswith "\\cscript.exe" or process.parent.executable endswith "\\mshta.exe" or process.parent.executable endswith "\\regsvr32.exe" or process.parent.executable endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or process.parent.executable endswith "\\wscript.exe")) or ((process.parent.executable like "*_\\AppData\\Local\\*" or process.parent.executable like "*_\\Users\\Public\\*" or process.parent.executable like "*_\\Windows\\Temp\\*")))))
